  "tagline": "Tiny TypeScript full-text, vector and hybrid search engine for browsers, servers and the edge.",
  "description": "Orama (originally Lyra) is an in-memory search engine written in TypeScript that runs in the browser, Node, Deno, Bun and edge runtimes with no native dependencies. It supports full-text search with typo tolerance, facets, filters, geosearch, vector and hybrid search, plus plugins for persistence, embeddings and documentation sites (it powers many docs search bars). The company behind it has since broadened into an enterprise AI platform (Metis), and the open-source library, now branded OramaJS, receives slower but continuing maintenance. Great for client-side and static-site search; not a server database.",
